<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.apache.logging.bench</groupId>
    <artifactId>log4j-bench-parent</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>bench-jdbc-jndi</artifactId>
  <name>Log4j Bench :: JDBC via JNDI</name>
  <description>The JDBC appender's DataSource connection source, resolved through an in-process JNDI context</description>

  <!--
    Runs on BOTH lines, which is the unusual part.

    On 2.x the DataSource connection source lives inside log4j-core. On 3.x it
    was split into log4j-jdbc-jndi, added by the profile below — so this module
    is one of the few places the split is directly observable: the same config
    works on both, and only the classpath differs.

    ── On enabling JNDI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Log4j has disabled JNDI by default since 2.17.0, with a separate flag per
    subsystem. This app needs log4j2.enableJndiJdbc=true, which ./bench passes
    for it and only for it.

    That is safe here for a reason worth stating rather than assuming: the JNDI
    provider is BenchInitialContextFactory, in this module, which resolves names
    from a HashMap populated by the application itself. It speaks no protocol
    and opens no socket, so there is no remote lookup to abuse. The flag is
    scoped to this one app, and the bench never sets enableJndiLookup — the
    ${jndi:} lookup that CVE-2021-44228 abused stays off everywhere, as
    configs/xml/lookups.xml demonstrates.
  -->

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-api</artifactId>
      <version>${log4j.api.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-core</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.h2database</groupId>
      <artifactId>h2</artifactId>
      <version>${h2.version}</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <profiles>
    <profile>
      <id>log4j-3x</id>
      <dependencies>
        <!-- 3.x moved DataSourceConnectionSource out of log4j-core. Without
             this the config still parses and the DataSource element is simply
             unknown, so the appender falls back to no connection source. -->
        <dependency>
          <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
          <artifactId>log4j-jdbc-jndi</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
          <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
          <artifactId>log4j-jdbc</artifactId>
        </dependency>
      </dependencies>
    </profile>
  </profiles>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
        <artifactId>exec-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <mainClass>org.apache.logging.bench.jndi.JdbcJndiBench</mainClass>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
